Feature: Mistral Vibe is reachable through the Intelligence Layer

  Everything Vibe needs to RUN already exists in this repo and is verified
  live: a `"vibe"` entry in the prompt engine's provider-capabilities with the
  correct real-agent shape, two production packs, and a dedicated launcher.
  What is missing is one layer up — the Intelligence Layer cannot ROUTE to it.
  `model_factory_lib.bb`'s `provider->agent` map has no `"mistral"` key, and
  the Model Steward's registry has no Mistral model at all, so no role
  recommendation can ever name one.

  This slice is those two registrations and nothing else. It does not touch
  the packs, the launcher, or the agent shape — all three already work.

  One thing it must NOT do is invent a model id. The other registry entries
  are real model strings (`anthropic/claude-sonnet-5`,
  `cerebras/llama-3.3-70b`, `openai/gpt-5.3-codex`), but the vibe packs carry
  no model at all — their per-role column is `--max-price`, a hard
  per-session dollar cap, and Vibe selects its own model. The id has to be
  read from the live tool, and when it cannot be, the entry is registered at
  agent granularity and says so.

  # BL-682 vibe-routing-01
  Scenario: the provider-to-agent map routes mistral to vibe
    Given the model factory's provider-to-agent map
    Then the mistral provider resolves to the vibe agent

  # BL-682 vibe-routing-02
  Scenario Outline: the existing provider mappings are unchanged
    Given the model factory's provider-to-agent map
    Then the <provider> provider resolves to the <agent> agent

    Examples:
      | provider  | agent  |
      | anthropic | claude |
      | openai    | codex  |
      | cerebras  | aider  |

  # BL-682 vibe-routing-03
  Scenario: an unknown provider still falls through to itself
    Given the model factory's provider-to-agent map
    When a provider with no mapping is resolved
    Then it resolves to its own name

  # BL-682 vibe-routing-04
  Scenario: the Model Steward carries a registered Mistral model
    Given the Model Steward registry
    Then it lists a model whose provider is mistral
    And that model carries a cost class

  # BL-682 vibe-routing-05
  Scenario: the registered model id is read from the tool, never invented
    Given the Model Steward registry
    Then the registered Mistral model id is traceable to the live tool's own report
    And an id the tool could not supply is registered at agent granularity with that reason recorded

  # BL-682 vibe-routing-06
  Scenario: registering Mistral leaves the other registry entries untouched
    Given the Model Steward registry before this slice
    When the Mistral model is registered
    Then every previously registered model keeps its status, context window and cost class
